{Your two knights and a pawn against his rook and three pawns. His b pawn is dangerous, but look how close your pieces are to his king on g3.}
41. b5 {He pushes his b pawn to go for the win, and that is a mistake: he has forgotten about his own king.} 41... Nf1+ {Check, and his king has only one square left. [%csl Gf3]} (41... Ne2+ {Checking from e2 lets his king slip out to g2.} 42. Kg2 Ne4 43. b6 {His king got out, and his b pawn runs on: you are lost.}) (41... Nh5+ {Checking from h5 moves the knight off f4, and his king walks out to g2.} 42. Kg2 Ne4 43. b6 {Your chance has gone, and his b pawn is too fast: you are lost.}) (41... Ne4+ {The check from e4 puts your knight where his rook can take it.} 42. Rxe4 Kxe4 43. b6 {You won his rook for a knight, but his b pawn is too fast for your last knight: you are lost.}) (41... Nd5 {Blocking the pawn with the knight on d5 gives him time to bring his rook over.} 42. Rd4 Ne4+ 43. Rxe4 {His rook takes your knight on e4, and even after you take back, his three pawns are too strong: you are clearly worse.}) (41... Nd3 {Sitting the knight on d3 gives no check, and his pawn runs.} 42. b6 Nc5 43. Ra5 {His rook guards the pawn from a5, and your knight cannot stop it: you are lost.}) 42. Kf3 42... g4# {Mate! Your pawn gives check on g4, and your knights and king cover every square around his king. He went for the win on the other wing and left his own king in a net. [%csl Ge3,Gg3,Ge2,Gg2]} (42... Nxh2+ {Grabbing the pawn on h2 with check lets his king out of the net.} 43. Ke3 Ng4+ 44. Kf3 {His king slipped out, and the mate has gone: the game is level.}) (42... Nd2+ {Another check, from d2, lets his king escape to e3.} 43. Ke3 Nb3 44. Ra3 {His king is out and his rook is active: you are clearly worse.}) (42... Ng3 {The knight on g3 gives no check, and his rook gets a check of its own.} 43. Rxf4+ gxf4 44. fxg3 {His rook took your other knight with check, and your pieces fell apart: you are lost.}) (42... Ke5 {Walking your king to e5 instead of mating gives him time.} 43. b6 Nxh2+ 44. Kg3 {His pawn runs on and his king escapes: you are lost.}) 0-1


