[FEN "2R5/8/6P1/8/8/3n1k2/5b2/2r2K2 w - - 0 69"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/2R5/8/6P1/8/8/3n1k2/5b2/2r2K2_w_-_-_0_69"]

{Your rook on c1 gives check, and his king on f1 is boxed in by your king and bishop. Keep that box in mind: here it matters more than counting pieces. [%cal Gf2e1,Gf2g1,Gf3e2,Gf3g2]}
69. Rxc1 {He has to take your rook: it is his only legal move.} 69... Nxc1 70. g7 {His pawn will queen next move whatever you do. Is there something better than stopping it?} 70... Nb3 {The quiet knight move! From b3 it reaches d2, where its check is mate, and his king has no square, so his only move is to make a queen. [%cal Gb3d2]} (70... Ne2 {The knight on e2 aims for mate on g3, but his new queen will guard g3 from g8. [%cal Ge2g3]} 71. g8=Q {His queen on g8 looks straight down the g column at g3, so there is no mate: only a draw. [%cal Rg8g3]}) (70... Bd4 {Attacking the pawn with the bishop comes too late, and it lets his king out of the box.} 71. g8=Q {His pawn queens anyway, and his king has room again: you are lost.}) (70... Ke3 {Walking your king to e3 opens the box: his king gets g2.} 71. g8=Q {His queen arrives with his king free to move: you are lost.}) (70... Nd3 {From d3 your knight has no mating check to give.} 71. g8=Q {His queen arrives, and your knight still cannot mate: you are lost.}) 71. g8=Q 71... Nd2# {Mate on d2! Your king and bishop cover every square around his king, and his new queen cannot reach d2. You let him have the queen because your mate came first. [%cal Gf2e1,Gf2g1,Gf3e2,Gf3g2]} (71... Nd4 {From d4 the knight gives no check, and his queen gets a move.} 72. Qf8+ {His queen starts checking your king, and you are lost.}) (71... Be3 {Moving the bishop to e3 gives his queen the time to act.} 72. Qxb3 {His queen takes your knight on b3, and you are lost. [%cal Rg8b3]}) (71... Ke4 {Stepping your king away to e4 leaves the knight on b3 hanging.} 72. Qxb3 {The new queen eats your knight, and the mate is gone for good: you are lost. [%cal Rg8b3]}) 0-1


[Event "Imbalanced endgames: let the knight go"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[Role "exercise"]
