s the pawn on g3, and only one runner is left: you are lost.}) 48. Rh8 48... g2 49. Rg8+ 49... Kh5 50. Rxg2 50... h1=Q {A new queen on h1: his rook could only stop one of your two pawns. He protected his pawn on e5 and let your king walk into g4. [%csl Gh1]} 0-1


