49. Na3 {The knight blocks on a3, and your king guards it. If his rook takes the knight, nothing stands between your pawn and a8. [%csl Ga3][%tail]} (49. Kb4 {Stepping off the a column abandons your pawn.} 49... Rxa7 {His rook takes the pawn on a7, and you are lost. [%cal Ra1a7]}) (49. Kb5 {Stepping to b5 leaves the pawn just as alone.} 49... Rxa7 {The pawn is gone, and so is the win: you are lost.}) (49. Kb3 {Your king slides to b3, and nothing shields your pawn on a7 any more.} 49... Rxa7 {His rook collects the pawn, and you are lost.}) 49... g5 50. a8=Q+ {A new queen on a8, with check, and your knight on a3 still blocks his rook. Your king chose a4 so that it could guard the knight, and the knight stopped the checks. [%csl Ga8]} 1-0


